                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have been giving this game a try and the result is this is absolutely Pay to Win, in the second region of the Campaign with several levels ahead of the monsters, I can barely make it thru, its absolutely Brutal. Considering you can pay to buy gems to buy random boxes for gears, chars and battle boosts... well that says it all, its a Pay to Win game, where if you don't pay or get unspeakably lucky, you won't be able to progress in either online or offline, because the enemies in the Campaign are OP and the only players to progress to the higher tiers of the Arena are payers. \n\nNow I know people will say you can win gems and thus buy some of those boxes... you win a gem or a couple per first wins in the Campaign at each of the 3 difficulties, and the match I did fight in the Arena I won 1, otherwise you get a few by completing achievements, the char box cost 200 gems, and the gear box cost 25 for a cheap one and 200 for a good one... and all of it a random boxes, so obviously you have low chances of getting anything descent and high chances of getting crap, you can't buy any chars or gear outside of those boxes which basically bind progress in large part to how much $ you are willing to throw at the game. So this game is going to quickly go nowhere for any Free Players, and considering I know how much those random box crap work from other games that all embraced that crappy gimmick, Payers are still likely to have to pay several hundreds of $ to get anything good.\n\nAlso said gear not only you again need to get lucky to get the good stuff, but also once equipped you can't unequip it without paying gems and if you don't know that and you try to replace the gear, it delete the one you used to have equipped... nice to learn wasting a blue 1 star item because they didn't say anything about that, considering again how rare those bleeding gems are... it would cost 50 gems to unequip a blue 2 star item from one of my char... which is twice the price of rolling the cheap random box... or a quarter of rolling for a char or good random box... how nice. \n\nAlso if your chars die you can either pay with those rare gems to revive them in battle, for 25 gems for all if all your chars died and to continue said battle, or after battle for a couple of gems each, unless you go back to your Barracks and pay gold... which while better if you got 2 chars killed you can say goodbye to quite a cut of your gold earned in that mission.",
